<title>USA: Kennedy-Wilson sees Q4 profit.</title>
<headline>Kennedy-Wilson sees Q4 profit.</headline>
<dateline>SANTA MONICA, Calif. 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kennedy-Wilson Inc said on Friday it expects to report a profit in the fourth quarter of about $480,000 or $0.39 a share, compared with a net loss of $2 million, or $1.43 loss a share a year ago.</p>
<p>In a statement, the company said revenues for the fourth quarter of 1996 are estimated to be $6.9 million, up from $3.4 million a year earlier.</p>
<p>For the year, the company said it expects to report a profit of $3.8 million or $2.91 a share versus a loss of $13.2 million, or $9.40 loss a share for 1995.  Revenues for 1996 are expected to reach $31.4 million, up from $20.6 million in 1995.</p>
<p>Final audited results are scheduled to be announced in March.</p>
